{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"doddered-undercover-alligator","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe src/rebar cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py:1-18, 67-129` — Preserve SIGTERM order, intake closure, grace bounds, and uvicorn backstop. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:1-16, 60-96, 122-127, 178-184, 251-281, 373-390, 501-542` — Preserve tool inputs/outputs, gate/force semantics, delivery fields, and workflow durability limit. Consumer: FastMCP; link-tool tests require all canonical relations.\n- `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:1-13, 79-108, 165-181, 298-355` — Preserve exclusive key genesis, read-only resolution, mismatch warning, principal/material binding, and signing behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py:1-13, 25-43, 101-207, 241-329` — Preserve signed subject binding, trusted-key order, authenticated material/manifest use, and replay prevention. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_operation_config.py:1-29, 54-65, 230-326` — Preserve immutable snapshot, provenance vocabulary, reentrancy, root matching, and context-local binding. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_proc.py:1-26, 46-61, 113-223` — Preserve whole-process-group reap sequence, store-root distinction, durable cwd choice, and detached-child contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/config.py:13-114, 167-239, 251-283, 472-555` — Preserve public compatibility exports, exact precedence, cache invalidation, snapshot binding, and malformed-config postures. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:1-21, 105-116, 409-447, 595-673, 694-711` — Preserve exposed surfaces, environment registry, path-load necessity, stateless transport, proxy security, and signer composition. Consumer: `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py` requires the module docstring to say reads are in-process.\n- `src/rebar/mirror_guard.py:1-26` — Preserve two monitored failure modes, output/exit behavior, and remediation. Consumer: argparse uses the module docstring as command description.\n- `src/rebar/secret_screen.py:1-34, 58-100` — Preserve refuse-not-redact policy, audited override, fixed-window entropy rationale, and whole-line PEM discrimination. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/signing.py:1-22, 69-145, 282-324, 375-405` — Preserve scheme dispatch, compatibility read path, attestation selection, and CLI verification contract. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"e95f-b385-d913-4c92","parent_id":"d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in src/rebar — cohort 03: mcp_serving–signing"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788570640563265637,"uuid":"87a6f912-c9c7-4f84-a6aa-a77ef01c6a8a"}